# GPU build (CUDA + NVSHMEM, MPI bootstrap), from the repository root:
cmake --preset default -DNVSHMEM_HOME=/path/to/nvshmem -DCMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES=90
cmake --build --preset default
ctest --preset default

# or with make, from tests/ (set NVSHMEM_HOME and ARCH, e.g. ARCH=sm_90):
make check -k -B

# single test (from root):
tests/run.sh tests/expr-elem/expr-elem 2

# CPU emulator (no GPU / CUDA / NVSHMEM / MPI needed), from root:
cmake --preset emulator && cmake --build --preset emulator && ctest --preset emulator
# or
tests/emulator/run_tests.sh                       # all tests
tests/emulator/run_tests.sh tests/expr-elem/expr-elem.cpp

# The number of processes is taken from the file name: name.N.cpp runs on
# N processes, otherwise 2.

# Tests use rmacxx::init / rmacxx::finalize instead of MPI_Init / MPI_Finalize
# (MPI is still available, e.g. MPI_Comm_rank, MPI_Wtime, MPI_Abort).

## Commented test cases
Some test cases were written for our test driven development workflow. They are partially enumerated here but, until they are actually implemented, they will be commented out and replaced with a noop main function. Some examples include:
 - dimensions/simple_gv_bulk_2D_subarray_ends_fail.2.cpp
